>
	<p>
		Hey there! I’m Akshay Sinha, a platform engineering, DevOps and AI enablement leader with 18+ years
		of experience building DevOps, SRE, cloud, automation and secure delivery platforms across financial
		services, media and enterprise technology. I like building practical platforms, simplifying complex
		systems, and helping engineering teams do their best work.
	</p>

	<h2>What I’m working on now</h2>
	<p>
		As Vice President of DevOps at Morgan Stanley, I lead DevOps, automation and production engineering
		for the Equity Swaps platforms in Institutional Securities. Lately that means putting GenAI to work on
		real engineering problems: an AI engineering assistant built on foundation models and RAG, grounded in
		Jira, incidents, change tickets and documentation; an AI-driven defect intelligence tool that cut manual
		defect analysis by around 60%; and developer tooling for data lineage and discovery built on Sourcegraph
		MCP and GitHub Search.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alongside that, I’ve built DevSecOps platforms on Airflow, Neo4j, GraphQL and Open Policy Agent, plus
		Kubernetes and OpenShift automation such as OPA-based admission controls and automated Kerberos
		provisioning.
	</p>

	<h2>How I got here</h2>
	<p>
		I started at Tata Consultancy Services in 2008, automating build, release and deployment for WebSphere,
		Java and .NET applications across India and the UK. At HCL Technologies I led DevOps for Comcast, NBC
		Universal and Universal Studios, working between India and the US. At Cognizant I led DevOps and platform
		teams for PepsiCo and Universal Studios, built a global NGINX-based API platform, and ran CDN operations on
		Akamai and Cloudflare.
	</p>

	<h2>On the side</h2>
	<p>
		I build things: <a href="/blog/2025-09-25-resume-builder/">SecureCV</a>, an AI-assisted resume builder
		for concise one-page resumes; HashtagHarvest, an AI-assisted platform that turns trending topics into
		content ideas; and local-first AI agents that run on open-source models on consumer hardware. I also mentor
		in the DevOps, platform engineering and cybersecurity communities and run workshops on OPA, platform
		security and engineering automation.
	</p>

